      "problem": "What is the area of a circle that has a diameter of $4?$",
      "worked_solution": "The radius of a circle is half the diameter. So, the radius of our circle is $r=2.$\n\nTherefore, the area is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2} \\\\  & =4\\pi .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
